# Jakarta Namespace Migration Guide

## Overview
Jakarta EE 9+ renamed all `javax.*` packages to `jakarta.*`. This is required for Spring Boot 3.x.

## Common Package Mappings

### Persistence (JPA)
```java
// Old
import javax.persistence.*;
import javax.persistence.Entity;
import javax.persistence.Table;
import javax.persistence.Id;
import javax.persistence.GeneratedValue;
import javax.persistence.Column;
import javax.persistence.Enumerated;
import javax.persistence.EntityNotFoundException;

// New
import jakarta.persistence.*;
import jakarta.persistence.Entity;
import jakarta.persistence.Table;
import jakarta.persistence.Id;
import jakarta.persistence.GeneratedValue;
import jakarta.persistence.Column;
import jakarta.persistence.Enumerated;
import jakarta.persistence.EntityNotFoundException;
```

### Validation
```java
// Old
import javax.validation.Valid;
import javax.validation.constraints.Email;
import javax.validation.constraints.NotBlank;
import javax.validation.constraints.Size;

// New
import jakarta.validation.Valid;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.Email;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.NotBlank;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.Size;
```

### Servlet
```java
// Old
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;
import javax.servlet.FilterChain;

// New
import jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;
import jakarta.servlet.FilterChain;
```

### Annotation
```java
// Old
import javax.annotation.PostConstruct;
import javax.annotation.PreDestroy;

// New
import jakarta.annotation.PostConstruct;
import jakarta.annotation.PreDestroy;
```

## Automated Migration
You can use find/replace or IDE refactoring:

```bash
# Using sed for batch replacement
find . -name "*.java" -exec sed -i 's/javax\.persistence/jakarta.persistence/g' {} \;
find . -name "*.java" -exec sed -i 's/javax\.validation/jakarta.validation/g' {} \;
find . -name "*.java" -exec sed -i 's/javax\.servlet/jakarta.servlet/g' {} \;
```

## Important Notes
1. Spring Boot 3.x automatically includes Jakarta EE 10 dependencies
2. No additional dependencies needed for jakarta.* packages
3. Some third-party libraries may still use javax.* - check compatibility
